<section class="faq-section" id="faq">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <h2 class="faq-title reveal">FAQ</h2>
    <div class="faq-list reveal">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is WellNest?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-a">WellNest is a personal health tracking app for people living with chronic conditions. Keep symptom logs, medications, appointments, care-team contacts, exercises, health expenses and reflections together instead of spreading them across separate apps.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I use WellNest as a chronic pain or CRPS diary?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-a">Yes. Record pain severity, location, pain types, duration, triggers and relief methods. Keeping dated entries helps you review what you experienced and bring a clearer history to discussions with your GP or pain specialist.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does WellNest include an asthma tracker and seizure diary?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-a">Yes. Asthma logs include symptoms, peak flow readings, triggers and inhaler use. The epilepsy tracker records seizure type, severity, duration and warning signs. You can keep these records alongside your medications and appointments.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I share my health records with my doctor?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-a">You can generate PDF reports for symptoms, medications, appointments and contacts, then share the relevant report with your care team. Reports organise the information you have recorded; they are not a diagnosis or a medical recommendation.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How do I get started with WellNest?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-a">Choose a plan on the pricing page, create an account and set up the trackers you want to use. WellNest is available on the web and on the Apple App Store. The pricing page shows current subscription options and trial details.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What does a chronic illness tracker app do?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-a">A chronic illness tracker keeps a dated record of your symptoms, flares, triggers, medications and appointments, so you can spot patterns over time and give your doctor an accurate history instead of relying on memory. WellNest adds condition-specific diaries for chronic pain, CRPS, asthma and epilepsy, plus an emergency plan and medical expense tracking.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How much does WellNest cost?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-a">WellNest Premium is AU$4.99 per month or AU$44.99 per year, and every plan starts with a 30-day free trial (no card needed).</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does WellNest replace medical advice?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p class="faq-a">No. WellNest is a record-keeping and organisation tool, not a diagnostic service or emergency monitoring system. Follow advice from your qualified healthcare professionals and seek urgent medical help in an emergency.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-links reveal">
      <a href="/Pricing">Compare WellNest plans</a>
      <a href="/appointment-prep-checklist">Prepare for an appointment</a>
      <a href="/PrivacyPolicy">Read our privacy policy</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

